{
  "area": "colombia-san-andres",
  "method": "San Andrés island and its fringing reef, plus Providencia and Santa Catalina in the Seaflower Biosphere Reserve. No official dive-site list exists: CORALINA and the Secretaría de Turismo publish no mooring or dive-site list, and the Old Providence McBean Lagoon plan names only its own zones (White Shoal for scuba, Crab Cay for snorkeling). Lists, one each: Karibik Diver's 21-site page (read through the Wayback Machine, 2019 snapshot; the live karibik-diver.com is gone), Divers Team's dive-point map of San Andrés (about 45 named points, a PDF read as an image through the Wayback Machine because the live site blocks fetching), Sea Pride Scuba's dive-points page, Gaia Scuba's article, and for Providencia Felipe Diving's site list (felipedivingshop.com) and The Dive Shop Old Providence's site list (23 sites). ProColombia and colombia.travel (the same national tourism board) count as one list: colombia.travel's adventure feature names San Andrés and Providencia sites, ProColombia's dive articles repeat and extend the San Andrés names. Read with no named sites: Banda Dive, Blue Life, Sirius Dive Shop, Anda di Wata, Karibik Diver today, and the Providencia shop Sonny (site is empty); Scuba San Andrés, San Andrés Divers, Sea Garden and Buzos del Caribe could not be read (dead, blocked or non-dive pages). PADI, DivePlannerPro, dive.site, Scuba Diving, Agenda del Mar and Colombian travel blogs, including blog.sanandresisla.travel, were leads only and never counted. A site is counted when it is on at least two independent lists and is a recreational scuba dive. Name matches judged by hand: Bajo Bonito is Karibik's Bajo Bonito and Divers Team's Plaza de Toros (PADI gives the alias); Diamond Cantil is Karibik's name for Divers Team's Cantil del Barco Hundido; Blue Diamond, Wreck Diamond and Barco Hundido are one wreck; Turtle Rock is Felipe's Piedra de La Tortuga and the shop's Turtle Rock; ProColombia's Trampa Tortuga is Divers Team's Trampa. Providencia's Canal Derecho and Canal Izquierdo may be Channel White and Blue but are kept as one-list rows. Most San Andrés rows rest on only the Divers Team map and Karibik; Banda, Blue Life, Sirius and Sonny publish no sites online. Counted 2026-10-14.",
